{
    "name": "@kitchensink/infra-security",
    "version": "0.0.0",
    "private": true,
    "type": "module",
    "//exports": [
        "Unlike the other shared @kitchensink/* packages, this one exports BUILT JS, not ./src.",
        "Its consumers are CDK app entrypoints, and prod-deploy runs four of them as COMPILED JS under",
        "plain `node` (e.g. `cdk deploy --app \"node packages/services/identity/infra/dist/bin/app.js\"`).",
        "A `main` of ./src/index.ts made that path fail with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: node type-strips",
        "index.ts but cannot resolve its `./x.js` relative imports, since no built .js sits beside them.",
        "Verified by running the real compiled entrypoint; see ADR-0013 and the integration suite in",
        "packages/infra/global/__tests__/cdk-nag-synth.integration.test.ts, which drives `node dist/bin/app.js`."
    ],
    "main": "./dist/index.js",
    "types": "./dist/index.d.ts",
    "exports": {
        ".": {
            "types": "./dist/index.d.ts",
            "default": "./dist/index.js"
        }
    },
    "scripts": {
        "build": "tsc -p tsconfig.build.json",
        "test": "vitest run",
        "lint": "eslint 'src/**/*.ts' --ignore-pattern '**/*.test.ts'",
        "typecheck": "tsc --noEmit",
        "format": "prettier --write .",
        "format:check": "prettier --check ."
    },
    "dependencies": {
        "cdk-nag": "^2.38.2"
    },
    "peerDependencies": {
        "aws-cdk-lib": "^2.176.0",
        "constructs": "^10.0.0"
    },
    "devDependencies": {
        "@kitchensink/eslint": "*",
        "@kitchensink/prettier": "*",
        "@kitchensink/typescript": "*",
        "@types/node": "^24.0.0",
        "aws-cdk-lib": "*",
        "constructs": "*",
        "eslint": "^10.0.3",
        "prettier": "^3.0.0",
        "typescript": "^5.9.3",
        "vitest": "^4.0.0"
    },
    "engines": {
        "node": "24.x"
    }
}
